        {
          "unit_id": "free_time",
          "title": "Friday Night Music",
          "description": "Habla de gustos y aficiones con like/love/hate + -ing y los pronombres objeto.",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "lesson_id": "free_time_lesson",
              "title": "like + -ing and object pronouns",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "phase": "context",
                  "type": "audio_context",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Friday night music",
                    "dialogue": [
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "This place is great! Do you like live music, Lucía?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "I love it! And I love dancing too."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Priya",
                        "text": "I don't like dancing. I like watching!"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "What do you do in your free time, Priya?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Priya",
                        "text": "I love cooking, and I like gardening. Our tomatoes are fantastic."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "And you, Daniel?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "I like running, and I love reading. But I hate shopping!"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Sam",
                        "text": "Hi, everyone! Do you like the band?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "We love it! You're brilliant, Sam!"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Sam",
                        "text": "Thanks! Daniel, nice to meet you. Lucía talks about you a lot."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "Really? Well, she talks about you too. And about your big black umbrella!"
                      }
                    ],
                    "passage": "Friday night at The Old Duke. Sam's band plays here every Friday. Tonight Lucía is with Priya and Daniel."
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "discovery",
                  "type": "multiple_choice",
                  "content": {
                    "instructions": "Fíjate en el diálogo y responde.",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "question": "\"I love dancing.\" After love/like/hate, the verb…",
                        "options": [
                          "takes -ing",
                          "takes -s",
                          "doesn't change"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"She talks about you.\" She talks about Sam → She talks about ___.",
                        "options": [
                          "he",
                          "him",
                          "his"
                        ],
                        "answer": 1
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "Who hates shopping?",
                        "options": [
                          "Daniel",
                          "Priya",
                          "Lucía"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "Who says \"I don't like dancing. I like watching!\"?",
                        "options": [
                          "Priya",
                          "Lucía",
                          "Sam"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "like / love / hate + -ing and object pronouns",
                    "explanation": "Para hablar de gustos: love (encantar), like (gustar), don't like (no gustar), hate (odiar). Si detrás viene una actividad, el verbo va en -ing: I love dancing, He hates shopping.\n\nOrtografía del -ing: dance → dancing (pierde la -e), run → running y shop → shopping (doblan la consonante).\n\nLos pronombres objeto van detrás del verbo o de una preposición: I love it, She talks about you, Come with me. Nunca «I love she»: se dice I love her.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Sujeto",
                        "Objeto",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "I",
                          "me",
                          "Come with me!"
                        ],
                        [
                          "you",
                          "you",
                          "She talks about you."
                        ],
                        [
                          "he",
                          "him",
                          "Do you like him?"
                        ],
                        [
                          "she",
                          "her",
                          "I like her."
                        ],
                        [
                          "it",
                          "it",
                          "We love it!"
                        ],
                        [
                          "we",
                          "us",
                          "Sam plays for us."
                        ],
                        [
                          "they",
                          "them",
                          "I love them."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "I love dancing.",
                      "Priya likes gardening.",
                      "Daniel hates shopping.",
                      "Do you like the band? — We love it!"
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "practice",
                  "type": "fill_blanks",
                  "content": {
